|---|---|---|
| **b** | Fixed 1.65-W RF/active beam, §2 ACM | Recommended conventional primary; angle changes received signal/rate, not transmitted watts. |
| **a** | Memoryless nominal target \(\gamma^\star=5.660030272\), from §2’s 8PSK 2/3 threshold; equal-airtime TDM, \(p_u=\min(1.65,\gamma^\star(N+\widehat I_u)/\widehat h_u)\) per simultaneous slot configuration | Preserves the earlier angle→RF intent; assumes a flexible, sufficiently fast payload controller. |
| **a′** | Same target, equal FDM subbands; each user’s RF ceiling \(1.65/n_b\), beam RF \(=\sum p_u\); subband noise/PSD/overlap computed consistently | L1 architectural alternative; never 1.65 W per simultaneous user. |

For a/a′, solve coupled nominal powers from a fixed history-independent initialization, with frozen convergence tolerance, iteration limit and residual certification before outcomes. No converged solution means INVALID, not silent cap-only success. Slot schedules/order and equal allocations are fixed design choices; no extra scheduler optimization or realized-channel access is permitted.

**Predeclared matrix: 18 cells = three architectures × the following six treatments.** This is a fractional 48-cell factorial with separate energy-factor contrasts and one combined-energy corner, not an exhaustive interaction study.

| Treatment suffix | Time integration | Standby | Useful-time interruption | Bits | Standalone physics cost relative to 302-s reference |
