U is an upper-bound diagnostic, ineligible as the paper’s primary. Its lowest-mode eligibility uses the zero-margin threshold; the power-controller target remains fixed to isolate the rate-model intervention. Every treatment has explicit formula-specific KAT expectations; U does not “pass” by claiming an SE cap it intentionally lacks.

**Priority fixed before results:** `b0 > a0 > a′0 > bS > aS > a′S > bH > aH > a′H > bSH > aSH > a′SH > bT > aT > a′T`; U cells are diagnostic only. This ordering favors conventional RF, integration accuracy and the stated partial-payload boundary before transferring ground-hardware/procedure proxies. Applicability labels are frozen before EE outcomes. The primary is the highest-priority eligible setting passing acceptance; a known implementation defect requires repair, not outcome-driven demotion. Snapshot models remain explicitly approximate.

**Parallel oracle work, before any training:**

- Use the same fresh TRAIN exogenous tapes across settings: four worlds × three fixed carriers—nearest-eligible, stay-if-possible and random-masked. Start with one prospectively indexed anchor per carrier/world, rotating the four refresh phases across worlds; include three forecast offsets. This deliberately bounded panel is a regime screen, not confirmation.
- Per cell, compute **E1 U₁**, **J₁**, and the union-catalogue optimum with complete candidate census and certificates. U and J are not nested; require a genuine multi-user witness exceeding the unilateral alternative before attributing a gain to joint coordination.
- Run **S0** with deployable nominal information, fixed top-two per-user proposals and the same frozen evacuation decoder. Also run NULL, random-feasible and nominal-greedy controls. Oracle-selected profiles must never become S0 inputs.
- Run exact-factor **FULL**, **DROP_C1**, **DROP_C2**, **DROP_C3**, and all-neutral controls. C3 is the set decoder; DROP_C3 executes the independent C1+C2 proposal. C1/C2 drops use prospectively fixed neutral centered scores in this oracle screen. Their learned successors instead use equal-budget neutral-source retraining: report these as different estimands.
- Evaluate all three \(\Delta_i=\eta_{\rm FULL}-\eta_{\rm DROP_i}\), not merely FULL versus BASE. E1 ceiling, factor-oracle composition and deployable S0 answer different questions; retain all three results.

**Report every cell as “where does coordination change EE.”** Required fields: applicability/KAT/certificate status; per-world and pooled U₁/J₁/union headroom; three DROP marginals; S0 gap; Δbits, Δjoules and their log-ratio decomposition; lit beams/satellites, PA/standby/circuit energy; decoding/useful-time availability, rate tails, outage runs and handovers; actual changed-user counts, nonadditive interaction, calibration values and decision-time tails. Name whether failure is absent physical headroom, bits sacrificed, energy not saved, proposal exclusion, decoder error, QoS loss or comparator strength.

**Stop rules and training admission:**

- Any integrity/KAT failure stops dependent work. INCOMPLETE/INVALID cells are not zero effects and cannot support the across-settings negative conclusion.
- Training admission uses the already selected primary, never the setting with the strongest C3. Retained factors require positive oracle marginals beyond certified numerical error and acceptable QoS. For C3, require genuine joint headroom and a deployable S0 gain; use the pre-existing Track B **1% practical deployment-gain threshold**, prospectively retained here.
- If oracle headroom exists but S0 fails, permit one fixed-budget decoder diagnosis and corrected integrity replay; then stop C3 progression if conversion still fails. No target/standby/margin retuning.
- **If C3’s set-level oracle marginal is ≤0 in every completed, physically defensible setting, close C3 training/screens/confirmation and report a bounded negative for this system class, panel and catalogue. Proceed with C1/C2 only, subject to their own gates.** An additive-head failure alone does not trigger this conclusion.
- Positive but subthreshold or inconsistent C3 effects are “insufficient practical evidence,” not mathematical impossibility. A positive secondary regime with a nonpositive primary remains a regime-map result; it does not replace the primary.

**Overnight cost and execution contract.** The [latency ledger](/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover-e1/.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-controller-handoff-20260907/LATENCY-LEDGER-2026-09-07.md:49) records **302 s on four workers for 3,840 composed evaluations**, excluding original E1 tape construction. Define \(q\) by a complete-suite rehearsal including new tape construction, coupled power, E1/S0/DROP scoring and certification; it is not yet measured.

| Cost quantity | Estimate / admission rule |
|---|---|
| One reference equivalent | \(302×4/3600=0.33556\) core-hours |
| Independent execution of all 18 cells | \(3(1+5×47)=708\) equivalents: **237.57q core-hours**; reject this execution strategy |
| Shared physical computations | Three architectures × (one snapshot + one 47-subinterval tape): **144 equivalents = 48.32q core-hours** |
| Planning case | \(q=2\), plus 30% orchestration/rescoring reserve: **125.63 core-hours**, approximately **6.28 h on 20 cores** |
| Overnight ceiling | **160 core-hours / 8 h** on 20 single-thread workers; require rehearsal \(q≤2.5\) with the same reserve |

Cache primitive geometry/channel/slot-power fields for the complete frozen catalogue; standby, blackout and rate treatments rescore those fields, then select independently. Share no outcomes or mutable arm state. Schedule architecture/world construction and cell scoring in parallel without nested thread pools. If the rehearsal misses the budget, optimize the shared computation before opening outcomes; do not quietly truncate catalogues or worlds. A deadline overrun yields INCOMPLETE and keeps the relevant training gate closed.

**After probe admission:**

1. **Stage A:** regenerate sources and train FULL2, DROP_C1, DROP_C2 and ALL_NEUTRAL with equal budgets and matched source strata; retain 100 source epochs as the inherited budget and use three independent initializations. Retrain the external MODQN comparator under the same successor objective. Add C3 learning only if its gate passes.
2. **Stage C ladder:** new, inventoried TRAIN-development worlds at **100→500→1500→3000**; early rungs check execution/integrity only. At 3000 issue a finite-panel GATE_PASS/GATE_FAIL with paired world/lineage uncertainty. Optional **6000→9000** continuation is pre-budgeted precision work, not another chance to obtain significance.
3. **C3-S screens:** fresh closed-loop worlds, learned-seed and greedy-seed comparators, S0 versus learned S3, NULL/random controls, actual joint moves and a 30.08-s deadline fallback. Recheck headroom against the newly trained strong BASE; disappearance is a valid comparator-strength falsifier.
4. **Confirmatory:** freeze the primary, policies, source/checkpoint selection, contrast family and stopping rule before opening an untouched panel. Use blocked/forward-time holdout with justified temporal separation, paired world inference and training-lineage replication; report multiplicity-adjusted component contrasts and QoS co-primaries. No favorable-rung selection.
5. **Campaign cost:** source-generation and fitting costs remain separate from physics evaluation. Price evaluation as \(L\,N\sum_a\tau_a/3600\) core-hours using a successor rehearsal. The inherited five-arm/three-lineage 3000-world estimate is approximately **140 core-hours at old speeds**; integration, revised forecasts and C3 search can raise it substantially. A 9000-world campaign approximately triples evaluation work; the overnight promise applies only to the oracle matrix.
6. **Running old work:** finish only already bounded attribution units that do not delay successor compute; checkpoint resource-competing diagnostics and stop expanding the old nine-arm matrix. Preserve every completed result, failure, source binding and unfinished status as **history only**. Do not reuse old positive/negative outcomes as successor gates.

