10. **Service.** For an allocated transmission, `served_PHY ⇔ SINR ≥ SINR_min`, with \(\mathrm{SINR}_{\min}=10^{-1.441812460/10}=0.7174947935\). Below it: zero decodable bits. NULL is unserved. Report time-weighted decoding availability and complete-service user-steps separately; this is not a minimum-throughput guarantee.
11. **Resolution order.** Fix assignments/airtime → radiate and compute joint interference → decode. Failed attempts retain RF energy/interference and their scheduled share; no retrospective pruning or bandwidth redistribution. Association legality is checked before execution; instantaneous decoding is checked afterward.
12. **Energy.** For interval pieces \(k\), \(E=\sum_k\delta_k\{\sum_{b\in\mathcal I_w}[z_{bk}(0.338+\max(P_{\rm idle},P_{\rm PA}(p_{bk})))+(1-z_{bk})P_{\rm idle}]+0.200N_{\rm active\,sat,k}+P_{\rm bus}\}\). An active satellite has at least one transmitting beam. Coefficients come from [the retained component model](/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover-e1/src/mcrl/env/link_budget.py:270); beam↔chain assignment is a benchmark assumption.
13. **Inventory/boundary.** \(\mathcal I_w\) is a manifest of physical NORAD/beam-chain identities fixed before actions and reused across arms and scored horizons; candidate slots do not define hardware. Primary \(P_{\rm idle}=0\), with ideal boundary switching; \(P_{\rm bus}=0\) denotes exclusion of bus, terminal, gateway and controller energy. Do not claim spacecraft EE or physically zero procedure energy.
14. **Standby sensitivity.** Use \(P_{\rm idle}=fP_{\rm PA}(1.65)\), \(f=35/420=1/12\), hence 0.698609768 W/chain. The cited ratio is from a ground Ka-band HPA’s mute/active prime-power ratings; transplanting it to this model is an engineering proxy, with flight applicability `VERIFY_SOURCE`. The active-floor clamp prevents “turn on at tiny RF to evade standby.” [CPI MKT-497, p.2](https://www.cpii.com/docs/datasheets/826/MKT-497%20SA49KOA_SB49KOA%2080%20W%20SSPA_SSPB.pdf)
15. **Handover.** No event-joule term. Primary interruption is zero; matrix interruption removes useful transmission time only, retaining scheduled RF draw. Separate same-satellite beam change, satellite change, reacquisition and initial entry; do not equate them automatically with RRC procedures.
16. **Interruption sensitivity.** Use 62/142 ms only as the conditional electronic-terminal/cell-handover scenarios recorded in [ADR-004:118](/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover-e1/docs/decisions/ADR-004-payload-boundary-time-only-c2.md:118); live beam→cell/procedure applicability is `VERIFY_SOURCE`. Clip blackout overlap exactly once; initial entry/re-entry are separately logged, not silently assigned 142 ms.
17. **Clock.** Decisions remain every \(47×0.640=30.08\) s, from [native constants](/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover-e1/src/mcrl/env/constants.py:73). Primary integration covers \([t,t+30.08]\): the value at \(t\) plus the next 47 D2 boundary samples define 47 trapezoidal intervals; handle known event discontinuities explicitly. Never apply the new action to pre-\(t\) samples.
18. **Geometry/state.** Advance mobility causally within each interval; rebuild D2 history chronologically. Wire the existing benchmark 10° elevation parameter into the live visibility contract; retain D2’s 1100-km threshold, 50-km hysteresis, 1.280-s TTT and 300-km altitude floor with their [scenario provenance](/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover-e1/src/mcrl/env/d2.py:76).
19. **Actions.** Retain 28 association actions, four cached satellite identities, seven local cells and four-decision refresh; these are candidate restrictions, not minimum residence. NO_OP remains legal exactly for an empty mask. Joint SINR is not an independently guaranteeable per-user legality mask; outage does not authorize hidden rescue.
20. **Observable information.** Policy inputs use current nominal geometry, D2 state and explicitly timestamped lagged telemetry. Remove independent “current CSI” noise and the false elevation fallback. Realized fading stays hidden from deployment selectors; forecasts use ephemeris/current motion assumptions, not future random realizations.
