## 3. Known-answer test suite

Use independent scalar calculations and synthetic worlds; parity between two calls to the production helper is insufficient. Constants below are either §2 values or explicitly synthetic fixture values.

1. **Joules/deduplication:** one active beam on one satellite for 30.08 s costs \((8.383317219+0.338+0.200)30.08=268.353221940\) J; adding a second user adds no PA/circuit charge.
2. **Bits:** synthetic \(W=12\) Hz, two equal-airtime users, two seconds, both at 8PSK 2/3: 19.80636 bits/user and 39.61272 total. Apply airtime, roll-off and duration exactly once.
3. **Handover-count invariance:** identical radiation, activation and geometry histories with different bookkeeping/event counts have identical E. Interruption changes B only. Actual moves to different physical states need not preserve energy in power-control alternatives.
4. **Lit-beam monotonicity:** at fixed \(P_b\), activating another beam on an already active satellite adds \((8.721317219-P_{\rm idle})\delta\) J; activating its first satellite beam also adds \(0.200\delta\).
5. **SE ceiling/table:** arbitrarily high SINR yields at most 3.710855833 bit/s/Hz; dominated table entries never displace a higher-efficiency eligible mode.
6. **Service boundary:** at \(\gamma_{\min}\), an allocated sample is served; the adjacent representable value below is not. Test NULL, partial-interval outage and nominal-pass/realized-fail separately.
7. **Pooling discriminator:** \((B,E)=(10,1),(10,9)\) gives pooled EE 2, versus mean ratios \(5.555\ldots\); duplication leaves pooled EE unchanged.
8. **Reward–endpoint identity:** for any fixed trajectory, \(\sum_tR_t=\sum_tB_t-\eta_{\rm ref}\sum_tE_t\). With \((B_{\rm ref},E_{\rm ref})=(100,10)\), the surplus-change sign matches the EE-change sign exactly.
9. **NULL≡BASE:** run the complete coordinator path but commit BASE; require identical actions, state, random keys, raw physics, B, E and service traces, excluding timing metadata.
10. **CRN matching:** world/user/NORAD/absolute-time/channel-component keys are identical across arms/settings; candidate reordering, duplicate evaluation and renewal do not reroll fading.
11. **RF consistency:** two equal-channel users on one fixed-RF beam both use 1.65 W in wanted fields; victims and PA accounting see that same transmission.
12. **TDM PA averaging:** equal 0.825/1.65-W slots give mean PA supply 7.155608836 W, not \(P_{\rm PA}(1.2375)=7.260165679\) W; overlapping beams follow the same slot clock.
13. **FDM conservation:** two equal subbands each receive \(W/2\), their own \(kTW/2\), consistent overlapping interference and RF allocations summing to at most 1.65 W.
14. **Memoryless control:** doubling isolated nominal channel gain halves required unsaturated RF; history changes do nothing. Exercise coupled convergence, cap binding, lower-MODCOD operation and solver failure without reused prior power.
15. **Standby inventory:** a dark chain contributes exactly \(0.698609768\delta\) J in the cited-proxy setting; changing candidate enumeration changes nothing. Tiny active RF cannot evade the standby floor.
16. **Interference/failed attempts:** synthetic wanted 10, intra 2, inter 3, off-colour 4 yields interference 5. A decoding failure does not remove its attempted beam from anyone else’s interference or energy.
17. **Time/causality:** \(R(t)=t\) over 30.08 s integrates to 452.4032 bits with trapezoidal samples; a terminal snapshot gives 904.8064. An action at \(t\) cannot change any pre-\(t\) receipt.
18. **D2/visibility/dwell:** latched 1000→1100-km history remains latched; short band-only initialization must not impersonate it. A 5° link fails the wired 10° mask; \(378/(4×30.08)=3.141\) refresh periods.
19. **Initialization/RNG:** world B alone or after A has identical initial state; changing scored horizon preserves initial state/common prefix; an evaluation call cannot alter the next training world.
20. **C2:** changing only segment-entry gain changes no successor feature/target. A projected loss remains absorbing in that forecast; live reconnection works. Verify three physical offsets even near the scoring endpoint.
21. **System externality:** focal +1 bit, nonfocal −10 bits, ΔE=0 gives immediate teacher surplus −9, not +1; a two-user evacuation must be distinguishable from singleton aliases.
22. **Independent reconstruction/mutations:** detect doubled bits, repeated PA/baseband charges, altered physical identities, stale source hashes and state pollution from counterfactual evaluation.
23. **Statistical/control discriminators:** exercise the common-floor ranking reversal above, missing all-neutral factorial cell, reused world IDs and arbitrarily tiny deterministic “passes”; none may silently become confirmatory support.
24. **Channel arithmetic:** independently check FSPL doubling-distance loss, \(kT_{\rm sys}W≈5.5754×10^{-13}\) W, S.465’s 2.04330° branch and Bessel accuracy; distinguish median-normalized shadow from unit-mean Rician power.
25. **Outage/deployment contract:** retain zero-bit/zero-energy dark steps in opportunities; an all-dark panel has explicit undefined EE, not dropped rows. All-false masks execute NO_OP; injected deadline misses execute the frozen BASE fallback.

