No constants or source files were modified. All arithmetic used only Python's standard math library through the user-specified interpreter with `-B` and `nice -n 15`.

## Independent follow-up: HOBS beamwidth provenance

Read-only extraction of the supplied local HOBS PDF confirmed Eq.3 on page2 and TableI on page6. Eq.3 is `mu(theta)=2.07123*sin(theta)/sin(theta_3dB)`, theta is the boresight angle, and the table gives theta_3dB=0.058rad. Its pattern therefore places the half-power boundary at about3.323155deg from boresight: the corresponding full span is about6.646310deg. V0.25 instead labels3.32deg a full HPBW and halves it, placing half power at1.66deg. This is a definition mismatch with the literal HOBS equation, not rounding. `NARROWER_IN_SOURCE` can describe the symbol's meaning (one-sided offset versus full angular span), while the resulting beam is physically wider in the source.

The legacy `env/antenna.py` header states that the project **registered**3.32deg as full HPBW. That is evidence of a project convention, not evidence HOBS uses it. The distinction is already documented in [proposed ADR-002](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-codex-ws-engine/docs/decisions/ADR-002-proposed-hobs-primary-geometry.md): its Context explicitly identifies the mismatch; its Alternatives rejects full3.32deg as a HOBS-faithful source claim while permitting it as a legacy sensitivity. Status is **Proposed**, so this ADR does not authorize geometry changes. It does establish that the current constants comment “retained HOBS full half-power beamwidth convention” is not supported by HOBS, even though the numerical project geometry itself has been declared and frozen. Report both facts; neither silently repairs nor silently source-verifies the current width.

HOBS source identity: Chen et al., *Energy-Efficient Joint Handover and Beam Switching Scheme for Multi-LEO Networks*, IEEE VTC2024-Spring, [DOI10.1109/VTC2024-Spring62846.2024.10683088](https://doi.org/10.1109/VTC2024-Spring62846.2024.10683088). Local PDF inspected: `.scratch/chinese-word-v023-lcsrs-20260905-r2/references-pdf/[04]_Energy_Efficient_Joint_Handover_and_Beam_Switching_S.pdf`. No source or geometry was changed.

