codex
The TDM energy calculation is an airtime-weighted sum of per-slot amplifier draw. Zero-bit and `NO_MODE` attempts keep their scheduled energy, and the old segment-anchored power reset is absent from this engine. The main formula concern is the slow solver certificate: a closed-form two-user example passes it while returned power is about 94% below the unique fixed point. This establishes a limit of the certificate, not an observed error in the project’s runs.
