251:`PA 252.170182580 + circuit 10.167040000 + processing 6.016000000 = 268.353222580 J` approximately; using unrounded component arithmetic gives **268.353221940 J**. At this operating point PA is 93.9695% of modeled energy. At the recorded low-power .014244 W example, PA is only 59.1469%, explaining why the .338/.200 coefficients matter more under aggressive power reduction. These are component-share arithmetic examples, not measured network averages.
286:**Verification limits and coverage.** The main file has 72 top-level assignments other than `__all__`; 71 are constant/metadata declarations and one is `__all__`’s helper-related accounting distinction checked in the inventory verification below. The completion check enumerated actual AST assignment names and numeric literals rather than trusting `PROVENANCE` coverage. Main tables cover every named constant, all 28 mode entries, the named/embedded defaults in the other five files, and the extra timing quantities requested by the user. String/schema constants are explicitly accounted for as declarations. Values that occur only as indices, neutral elements or guards are not presented as hardware claims.
288:The exact TS 38.133 interruption anchors could not be independently read: the official PDF exceeded the web parser’s document-size limit, and the permitted shell could not resolve ETSI’s hostname. [Local R2 provenance matrix][R2] and [ADR-004][ADR4] supply exact claimed clauses and meanings, but neither was promoted to primary evidence. Consequently the source-anchor verdict remains `UNVERIFIABLE_HERE`, while the conditional model adoption is acknowledged as `DECLARED`. No physical source was found for the operational 20-s attribution; the 10-s compute target and 30.08-s arithmetic are declared and valid as such.

