+**All 28 code-table entries.** Each row gives the exact declared triple. The quoted common provenance is “EN 302 307-1 V1.4.1 Table 13, normal FEC frames, no pilots”; the source definition is the DVB evidence row above. `e` is bit/symbol, `g` is ideal Es/N0 dB, and the last column is derived model bit/s/Hz. All comparisons below are `MATCHES` for the **table transcription**, not a claim that the 1.7 dB adoption was standardized. [Table 13][DVB]
