+
+The reported result with the largest directly calculable exposure to the first item is the **2° endpoint of the existing off-axis power/EE figure**. Its recorded 1.112370 W and 9.174814 Mbit/J become, by isolated-link arithmetic with every other fixture input held fixed, 1.65 W and **zero decodable bits/zero EE** when width is halved, or 0.511755 W and **13.076999 Mbit/J (+42.53%)** when width is doubled. Energy changes from 223.233550 J to 268.353222/156.620513 J. This is a sensitivity of the recorded, unreserved single-user fixture, not a rerun of the current quantile-controlled network or an estimate of FULL-versus-DROP gains. Network-wide changes cannot be quantified from constants alone. [Recorded figure receipt][FIG]
+
+`DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM` — 2026-09-09. Read-only source examination and arithmetic; **no simulation, test suite, production engine import, random draw, training or replay was run**. The source checkout is `/home/sat/mcrl-v025-codex-ws-engine`, HEAD `75c5c78cac3833e5a3100bf948211023d0de228c`. File hashes below identify the actual examined bytes, including the possibility of an existing dirty checkout. No replacement values are proposed.
+
+The lead table contains every adverse or unavailable **source verdict** in this audit, ordered by calculable conditional PHY sensitivity: beamwidth, 142-ms interruption, then 62-ms interruption. The requested timing attribution follows because it has no direct PHY effect and its operational effect cannot be quantified. Numerical solver assurance is a separate formula finding below: its constants are declared algorithm choices, yet its slow certificate does not bound solution error.
+
+`MATCHES` means that the number and the cited source’s definition agree for the stated component or benchmark. It does not mean calibrated flight hardware. `DECLARED` means an explicit model, engineering or computational choice; a source may substantiate an ingredient without substantiating its transplant. `UNVERIFIABLE_HERE` distinguishes inaccessible evidence from no evidence. An assertion in `PROVENANCE`, `VERIFY_SOURCE`, a test, or an older review was treated as a claim to trace, never as independent source confirmation.
+
+**Sensitivity convention.** Unless stated otherwise, each row changes that declared numeric quantity to ½/2 of its value, holding geometry, assignments and unrelated constants fixed, and propagating its intended algebraic dependants. For dB-valued quantities this means halving/doubling the **dB number**, not ±3.0103 dB; the distinction is explicit where material. Discrete counts may make a hypothetical input invalid. For a fixed trajectory, if a component contributes energy fraction `s`, multiplying that component by `f` gives `E′/E = 1 + (f−1)s` and `EE′/EE = 1/[1+(f−1)s]`, provided bits do not change. In an isolated, uncapped link at fixed target, `p ∝ N/g` and PA supply `∝ √p`; coupled links have no universal percentage bound. Modes, cap hits, outages, selection and trajectories can change discontinuously. Those caveats apply to every local sensitivity below.
+
+**What the primary sources establish.**
+
+| Evidence | Verified source definition and its limit |
+|---|---|
+| SI | Speed of light in vacuum and Boltzmann constant have exactly the declared SI values, with no uncertainty. [BIPM defining constants][SI] |
+| DVB-S2 | Table 13 has 28 normal-frame, no-pilot entries: efficiency per symbol and ideal AWGN `Es/N0` at quasi-error-free PER `10⁻⁷`. The test assumes perfect synchronization/carrier recovery, no phase noise and 50 LDPC iterations. These are not a measured universal hard-decoding law in satellite interference. The project declares that abstraction. [EN 302 307-1 V1.4.1, §6, p. 36][DVB] |
+| Common margin | 1.7 dB is the upper reported **32APSK AWGN implementation loss**; the source reports different ranges by constellation and treats nonlinear satellite degradation separately. Its test roll-off is 35%. A common 1.7 dB at the project’s 20% roll-off is a declared adoption. [BO.1784-1, Attachment 1 to Annex 1, §1][BO] |
+| RF/baseband | You et al. separate PA supply from the RF chain. The 338 mW chain sum is DAC 300 + mixer 19 + low-pass filter 14 + baseband amplifier 5 mW. `P_BB = 200 mW` is digital baseband precoder power. Neither supplies all payload/platform overhead. The Ku-band paper uses different PA parameters; it does not source this engine’s 0.35 or 5.2178 W. [You, Table II][YOU1], [You, Eqs. 12–15 and numerical setup][YOU2] |
+| Standby proxy | CPI specifies whole ground Ka-band SSPA/BUC prime power: 420 VA typical at linear rated output, 35 VA muted, with 48 VDC input. This is not a per-spacecraft-PA bias measurement. The ratio is real; transferring it to a chain is declared. [CPI MKT-497, p. 2][CPI] |
